From: OCCTSwift ecosystem <noreply@secondmouse.au>
Subject: [PATCH] Modeling Algorithms - a chamfer with parallel spine tangents is
 declined: no infinite extension, no walk over a non-finite range, no invalid result

BRepFilletAPI_MakeChamfer on the model attached to OCCT#1576 (FreeCAD#21369) at distance 1 on any
of 12 of its 36 edges is a SIGSEGV in Extrema_GGExtPC::Perform, under
BRepBlend_Walking::CorrectExtremityOnOneRst, with the walk's Pmax = -inf, Fleche = inf and a NaN
point. Three changes, one defect chain.

1. ChFi3d_ChBuilder.cxx, ExtentSpineOnCommonFace (reached from ExtentTwoCorner). It extends the two
   chamfer spines meeting at a vertex by dis / tga, tga = sinalpha / (cosalpha + dis2 / dis1). For
   parallel spine tangents (cosalpha = 1, sinalpha = 0) tga is 0 and the extension is +infinity,
   which passes "if (d1plus > 0.)" into Spine->SetFirstParameter(-inf). A non-finite extension is
   now no extension.

2. BRepBlend_Walking.cxx, Perform. The infinite ElSpine range becomes wf and wl in
   ChFi3d_Builder::PerformSetOfSurfOnElSpine and from them Pmax and Fleche; CorrectExtremityOnOneRst
   then builds Extrema_ExtPC over that range with a NaN point. OCC_CATCH_SIGNALS is inert in this
   build, so no bridge catch reaches the signal. Perform now returns with done = false when the
   start, the end or Fleche is not finite, the state every caller (ComputeData and its siblings)
   already tests with IsDone().

3. BRepFilletAPI_MakeChamfer.cxx, Build. With only the first change, the 12 edges that crashed are
   declined, but edges 1 to 12, which the pinned kernel declined because their infinite range made
   the walk fail, are built as BRepCheck-invalid shapes of negative volume (-754972), like edge
   15's -775000 on the pinned kernel. Build now reports a result that is not a valid solid,
   or does not become valid under the SameParameter pass callers apply next, as not done, which is
   what BRepFilletAPI_MakeFillet::Build does in the fillet series (the same isValidResult test).

Found by instrumenting the pinned kernel with override-linked copies of BRepBlend_Walking.cxx,
ChFi3d_Builder_2.cxx and ChFi3d_ChBuilder.cxx (Scripts/repro/3350-chamfer-extrema-sigsegv/): the
first print is "cos=1 sin=0 dis1=1 dis2=1 d1plus=inf d2plus=inf" and everything downstream
(Pmax=-inf, Fleche=inf, hguide first=-inf last=inf) follows from it. On the OCCT#1576 model,
chamfer d = 1 on each of the 36 edges one at a time: 12 SIGSEGV before, all 36 declined after,
including edge 15, which was a done chamfer of volume -775000 that BRepCheck rejects.

Tracked as SecondMouseAU/OCCTSwift#3350.

